          "componentAttributes": {
            "richTextValue": "<div class='ph-res'><h2>How to get help</h2><div class='ph-grid'><div class='ph-card'><h3>Emergency</h3><p>Fire, a gas leak, a flood, or a total loss of power or heat: call the 24/7 hotline first. Do not use the portal as the emergency response.</p></div><div class='ph-card teal'><h3>Routine repairs</h3><p>A dripping faucet or another routine repair goes through the resident portal. The target response is 48 to 72 hours, and staff record a low-priority case.</p></div><div class='ph-card indigo'><h3>A leak that is spreading</h3><p>Water coming through a ceiling, pooling across a floor, or a leak that is getting larger is not routine. Call the 24/7 hotline.</p></div><div class='ph-card teal'><h3>Office closed</h3><p>A non-emergency report can still be saved as a case when the office is closed. The routine target stays 48 to 72 hours.</p></div><div class='ph-card indigo'><h3>Repeated repairs</h3><p>Pacific Haven recommends replacement when the same type of repair for that resident has more than three closed cases in the past 365 days.</p></div></div></div>"
          },
